  "body": "> > is it possible to delay the apperance of the message\n> \n> what I can do is suppress the error message if no file name is selected. I think this makes sense in general.\n> \n> You can customize the duration by changing the value of `ErrorMessageDuration` in the `options` file (usually under something like `C:\\Users%username%\\AppData\\Local\\ART\\options` on windows) while ART is not running. The specifies the duration of such messages in milliseconds\n\nI can change the value of `ErrorMessageDuration` by reducing it, but this could not be smart in other cases.\nSo I suppose that the introduction of another variable, something like `ErrorMessageDelay` could be useful!\n\nRegards,\nTopoldo\n\n\n",
